  abstract = {Data association is a fundamental and challenging problem in multi-target multi-sensor tracking.It is even more challenging in the context of sensor networks.The paper proposed a classification-aided data association technique based on graphical models to efficiently solve such data association problems.The classification likelihoods based on the confusion matrix is used to modify node compatibility functions and edge compatibility functions of the data association algorithm based on graphical models.The simulations of multi-target tracking in the sensor networks environment,the comparison of results showed classification information improve data association.},
}

